# OAuth — Every Grant Type

Unlike everything else in this repo, **this file cannot run against a free, zero-setup public API** — OAuth inherently needs a registered client (a real `client_id`/`client_secret`, a real token endpoint, sometimes a real redirect URI). This is a **fill-in-your-own-credentials template**, meant for local manual testing only, never for CI. Every `OAUTH_*` variable below is a placeholder — replace with your own provider (Auth0/Okta/Keycloak dev tenant, your own backend, a GitHub/Google OAuth app, etc.) before running anything here.

The destination for every section is deliberately still `{{HTTPBIN_URL}}/bearer` — not because httpbin is a real protected resource (it accepts any token), but because it's a convenient, inert place to **see** what the OAuth2 flow actually produced. Run with `--show-req` and check whether a real `Authorization: Bearer <token>` shows up — that's the actual thing being tested here, not httpbin's response.

Two of five grants are decorated as `/tool` — the two that are fully headless (no browser, no human in the loop) and therefore realistic for an agent to call. `authorization_code` and `implicit` both require an interactive browser redirect and can only be exercised from the **Voiden app itself**, not headlessly or by an agent — see each section's note.

