  colorIndex: 1
  label: "OAuth2 — Password Grant (tool-friendly, legacy)"
---
```

Resource owner password credentials — the client holds the user's actual username/password and trades them directly for a token. Increasingly disabled by providers (it's deprecated in OAuth 2.1) — include it because the skill documents it and some internal/legacy systems still use it, not because it's a recommended pattern for anything new.

