```void
---
type: request-separator
attrs:
  uid: "90a9591c-5c31-4655-adff-e51e7fd9880a"
  colorIndex: 4
  label: "OAuth1 (tool-friendly, legacy)"
---
```

The odd one out among the "legacy" grants: OAuth 1.0a is fully headless **once you already have an access token/secret pair** (the three-legged handshake that issues them is a one-time, out-of-band setup step, not something re-run per request) — so unlike authorization_code/implicit, it's realistic to decorate as a `/tool`. Signature computed per-request from `consumer_key`/`consumer_secret`/`access_token`/`token_secret` — no token endpoint call needed at request time.

