## Local testing steps

1. Pick a real OAuth provider for the grant(s) you're testing — a free Auth0/Okta dev tenant is the easiest way to get all four OAuth2 grants against one provider without standing up your own; Keycloak (self-hosted, free) if you want full control including the password grant, which many hosted providers disable by default.
2. Add the real `OAUTH_*` values to `.voiden/env-private.yaml` (gitignored — never commit these) or `--env-var` overrides. Never put real client secrets in `.voiden/env-public.yaml` or `.env`.
3. For `client_credentials`, `password`, and OAuth1: run the section directly (`voiden-runner run local-testing/oauth-scenarios/oauth-every-grant-type.void --show-req`) and check whether a real `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (or OAuth1 signature) shows up on the request to httpbin — that confirms the token round-trip actually happened.
4. For `authorization_code` and `implicit`: open this file in the **Voiden app**, fill in the row values, and use the app's interactive OAuth flow (there is no headless equivalent).
5. Once you have real credentials, flip each `mode: none` to `mode: live` and re-run `tool verify` / `mcp serve --check` to see these three tools move from "not evaluated" to actually verified or failing.
